 prediction markets. Rating outlets broadly place the race in the Safe or Solid Democratic column, though a few call it Likely Democratic. Markets give Costa roughly a 95% chance of winning. The combination of incumbency, fundraising dominance, and a favorable district points to a comfortable Costa victory, with the main uncertainty being turnout dynamics in a low-information down-ballot race.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.9799, "margin": 14.05}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.9726, "margin": 13.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.9754, "margin": 14.0}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.9684, "margin": 13.5}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.9588, "margin": 13.0}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.957, "margin": 13.5}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.9737, "margin": 14.0}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.9821, "margin": 14.0}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.9693, "margin": 14.0}, {"date": "2026-10-01", "p_dem": 0.9851, "margin": 15.0}, {"date": "2026-10-02", "p_dem": 0.977, "margin": 14.0}, {"date": "2026-10-03", "p_dem": 0.9684, "margin": 14.0}, {"date": "2026-10-04", "p_dem": 0.9786, "margin": 14.5}, {"date": "2026-10-05", "p_dem": 0.9724, "margin": 14.5}]}